{
  "configuration_id": "config_010",
  "reason": "With only one completed experiment (config_016: multimodal, singleprofile, pca_n2000, resnet50, concat → acc 0.527), we have almost no evidence about which design choices matter. The most critical uncertainty is the standalone contribution of each modality, since the low multimodal accuracy could stem from a weak individual modality, poor fusion, or both. Config_010 (image_only, singleprofile, resnet50) is the cleanest single-variable ablation of the RNA component from config_016, isolating the image modality's performance with the same encoder and profile setting. If image alone performs comparably to the multimodal result, the RNA modality or fusion is the bottleneck; if it performs substantially better, RNA with PCA may be adding noise; if it performs worse, the multimodal combination is providing some benefit. Establishing this baseline is essential before investing further experiments in more complex multimodal variants (different encoders, multiprofile, transformer aggregation, weighted fusion), as it determines whether the image modality is even a viable signal source and guides which multimodal dimensions to prioritize next."
}

